@format 1
@id section-modification.common.compass-buttons
@title Compass buttons
@section Section modification
@area Common
@entry start-button,split-button,end-button
@summary Map the Split Compass Start, Split, and End buttons when they modify an already selected section; the Split operation is included because it necessarily shortens the original section while creating the right half.
@related section-modification.set-start-on-selected-section, section-modification.split-selected-section, section-modification.set-end-on-selected-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag compass

@alias compass = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PCompass
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[start-button] Start button Click <input>
- The Split Compass Start button invokes the supplied setStart action, which dispatches the section-start command @ compass.PCompass(...) / Start button Click lambda
> start-dispatch

[split-button] Split button Click <input>
- The Split Compass Split button invokes the supplied splitSection action, which dispatches the section-division command @ compass.PCompass(...) / Split button Click lambda
> split-dispatch

[end-button] End button Click <input>
- The Split Compass End button invokes the supplied setEnd action, which dispatches the section-end command @ compass.PCompass(...) / End button Click lambda
> end-dispatch

[start-dispatch] Submit setStart to the active flow <process>
- Invoke PFlowShortcutDispatch with setStart; the called map follows only the existing-section modification branch @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setStart
> map:section-modification.set-start-on-selected-section

[split-dispatch] Submit splitSection to the active flow <process>
- Invoke PFlowShortcutDispatch with splitSection; the called map follows the existing-section modification inherent in a successful split @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / splitSection
> map:section-modification.split-selected-section

[end-dispatch] Submit setEnd to the active flow <process>
- Invoke PFlowShortcutDispatch with setEnd; the called map follows only the existing-section modification branch @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setEnd
> map:section-modification.set-end-on-selected-section
